data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Start with the adjoint of the loss, which is 1. For `L = r * r`, the adjoint that reaches `r` is\n`2 * r`, because both factors are `r`. Each later step then passes its adjoint to its inputs:\nthe local derivatives of `y = q + e`, `r = y - t`, `z = p + b` and `h = tanh(z)` are 1, -1, 1 and\n`1 - h*h`. `h` and `w` each have two consumers, so each collects two terms."},"hints_note":null}

